# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Generated index — rebuilt by `python -m assistant.index`. Not committed: it is
# tied to the embedding model on the machine that built it.
data/index/

# data/embeddings.db IS committed, deliberately — decision 17. It is keyed by
# content hash and model tag, so it either hits correctly or misses and
# recomputes, and it turns a fifteen-minute first build into a few seconds.

# Captured diagnosis cases, written at runtime whenever a question hands off to
# the technical team. Two hundred of them accumulate from a single test run,
# they are regenerated on every run, and the ones a test produces carry
# `expert_diagnosis: null` and `example.invalid` chunk ids -- capture noise
# rather than the labelled library decision 16.1 describes. A real library is
# built by advisors correcting real photographs, and that is partnership work
# with its own distribution decision to make.
data/failure_library/

# Evaluation output that is regenerated on each run
eval/results/*.tmp

# Secrets. deploy/.env.example is committed; deploy/.env never is.
.env
deploy/.env
*.env
!deploy/.env.example

# Tooling
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Coverage output, regenerated on every run
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/
.coverage.*
.pipeline-*.txt

# The content-addressed source archive. Regenerated by every index run and, at
# present, 94 of its 95 files are byte-identical to an original already shipped
# under data/cache/pages and data/cache/documents. Committing it doubles the
# corpus in history to protect against a fetch that overwrites a file the
# database still points at — a real risk, but one that only bites a deployment
# that re-crawls, and such a deployment builds its own archive on first run.
data/cache/versions/

# Test and tooling output. None of this existed when the rules above were
# written; `tests/e2e/` drives a real Chromium now, and Playwright's default
# reporters drop both of these in the repository root on a failure.
.pytest_cache/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Log output. `.env.example` suggests OTEL_LOG_FILE=logs/app.jsonl, which would
# otherwise land in the working tree untracked and unignored.
*.log
logs/

# Editor state
.vscode/
.idea/
